   "text": "# Marburg virus disease - Rwanda\n\nWHO reports 66 confirmed cases of Marburg virus disease in Rwanda.\n\n## Situation at a glance\n\nAs of 28 October 2026, a total of 66 confirmed cases of Marburg virus disease, including 15 deaths, have been reported in Rwanda. The case fatality ratio among confirmed cases is 23% (15/66).\n\nSince the last update, 1 444 contacts have been listed and 1 210 of them have completed follow-up.\n\nParagraph 1: response teams continue contact tracing, infection prevention and community engagement in the affected districts; no new information on case numbers is given here.\n\nParagraph 2: response teams continue contact tracing, infection prevention and community engagement in the affected districts; no new information on case numbers is given here.\n\nParagraph 3: response teams continue contact tracing, infection prevention and community engagement in the affected districts; no new information on case numbers is given here.\n\nParagraph 4: response teams continue contact tracing, infection prevention and community engagement in the affected districts; no new information on case numbers is given here.\n\nParagraph 5: response teams continue contact tracing, infection prevention and community engagement in the affected districts; no new information on case numbers is given here.\n\nParagraph 6: response teams continue contact tracing, infection prevention and community engagement in the affected districts; no new information on case numbers is given here.\n\nParagraph 7: response teams continue contact tracing, infection prevention and community engagement in the affected districts; no new information on case numbers is given here.\n\nParagraph 8: response teams continue contact tracing, infection prevention and community engagement in the affected districts; no new information on case numbers is given here.\n\n### Cases by district\n\nTable 1. Confirmed cases and deaths by district\n\n| District | Confirmed cases | Deaths |\n